1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,450
The man responsible for thousands of deaths left the country the same day.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:11,390
7 December 1984. Union Carbide's chairman, Warren Anderson, arrived in Bhopal.

3
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,330
He was arrested.

4
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,690
But he was held for only a few hours, at the company's guest house.

5
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:23,010
He got bail the same day, and was flown out on a government plane.

6
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:26,870
He never came back to face trial.

7
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:33,050
The court declared him an absconder. He died in the USA in 2014.

8
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,910
Most of the victims received only 25,000 rupees,

9
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,970
and that too, years later.

10
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:42,550
For the full story of the fight for justice, subscribe.

